    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "a12d4488-9ea1-3ccd-bfc7-562cb22207ed",
                "word": "apographic",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "447c3334-1f07-3b99-a113-2bc7679c94df",
                        "entry_id": "a12d4488-9ea1-3ccd-bfc7-562cb22207ed",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of or relating to the apograph of a manuscript."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cd248674-ad2c-42c6-b2d0-dd0f0a131be9",
                                "sense_id": "447c3334-1f07-3b99-a113-2bc7679c94df",
                                "text": "At the same time, we must recognize that any translation, however good, cannot be accorded the status of the autographic or apographic texts."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c8017c14-6e41-4708-9bb7-a7defec1078e",
                                "sense_id": "447c3334-1f07-3b99-a113-2bc7679c94df",
                                "text": "According to Westminster, the originals that were the final arbiter were the apographic texts, not the original autographs that nobody has."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e8d46d73-8064-4b67-9e04-9b5c0413e2d2",
                                "sense_id": "447c3334-1f07-3b99-a113-2bc7679c94df",
                                "text": "At first glance, the editions of Bach's works from his lifetime would seem to be as immutable as fair apographic copies of other works of the composer."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6179c90b-269e-4217-a567-09a1b72c3531",
                                "sense_id": "447c3334-1f07-3b99-a113-2bc7679c94df",
                                "text": "Consequently, a common trace in old and modern document witnesses, as well as in autographic and apographic materials, is their elliptical nature for even if a large dossier génétique has been kept, it only represents a rather small part of the whole making process leading from a mental project to a self-contained work."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cb070d9f-b38a-37ea-b146-82e73fd1ce10",
                        "entry_id": "a12d4488-9ea1-3ccd-bfc7-562cb22207ed",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Fine-grained."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "092e261a-3632-47e1-9315-9d597f7b7c88",
                                "sense_id": "cb070d9f-b38a-37ea-b146-82e73fd1ce10",
                                "text": "Apographic structures include a number of varieties: feathery or dendritic, augen, gneissose, ichthyoglyptic, etc."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9a0f69e9-a821-4d29-b427-2614ce4961ca",
                                "sense_id": "cb070d9f-b38a-37ea-b146-82e73fd1ce10",
                                "text": "[…] the formation of the \"stuffed ” variety is spatially and genetically closely related to the incomplete albitization of the graphic and apographic pegmatite."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
